# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Android / Bubblewrap
#
# android/.gitignore covers these too; repeated here so the rules still apply
# if key material is ever created outside android/. Losing android.keystore
# means losing the ability to update the Play listing, and leaking it means
# someone else can sign builds Android accepts as Zero Club.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
*.pepk
keystore.properties
android/.build/
android/.twa/
android/out/

# Build logs can capture tool output that includes signing passwords.
build-log.txt
*-build-log.txt

# Generated PWA output. Regenerated by every build, so tracking it only
# produced merge conflicts over files nobody edits.
dev-dist

# One-off investigation scripts and error dumps belong in a scratch directory
# outside the repo, not committed. They were 56 files and 628KB of noise that
# made the project look like a scratchpad.
/check_*.ts
/check_*.js
/scratch_*
/ts_errors*.txt
/temp.tsx
/*.log
